e and Hudson.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d3d76e902037c862bbf782cd6c4ef6edb8a6951a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d3d76e902037c862bbf782cd6c4ef6edb8a6951a.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-104.73,38.02],[-104.88,38.05],[-104.89,38.25],[-104.62,38.19],[-104.73,38.02]]]},"properties":{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 22 at 4:43PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 443 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 12\nmiles south of Pueblo Reservoir, or 15 miles southwest of Pueblo,\nmoving north at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSouthwestern Pueblo.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.44de2db7efb2e67e1631a853032a451057c52c95.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.44de2db7efb2e67e1631a853032a451057c52c95.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-105.2,38.88],[-105.13,38.94],[-104.99,38.87],[-105.15,38.76],[-105.2,38.88]]]},"properties":{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 22 at 4:40PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 439 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nPikes Peak, or 16 miles west of Colorado Springs, moving southeast at\n10 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nPikes Peak.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4b3642c5bbdd1a6a71f13b8f56e37aaed57511a4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4b3642c5bbdd1a6a71f13b8f56e37aaed57511a4.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-104.9,40],[-104.88,40.17],[-104.54,40.07],[-104.78,39.82],[-104.91,39.85],[-104.9,40]]]},"properties":{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 22 at 4:22PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 422 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nBarr Lake, or 15 miles northeast of Denver, moving northeast at 25\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nCommerce City, Brighton, northwestern Denver International Airport,\nFort Lupton, Lochbuie, Hudson, Barr Lake, Todd Creek, Wattenburg\nand Henderson.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Central and South Weld County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2921140a76dcbd9cc0960c9fd28cc956f95adf0f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2921140a76dcbd9cc0960c9fd28cc956f95adf0f.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-105.17,39.41],[-105.17,39.42],[-105.12,39.48],[-105.08,39.57],[-105,39.6],[-104.93,39.53],[-105.04,39.45],[-105.04,39.36],[-105.06,39.32],[-105.14,39.34],[-105.17,39.41]]]},"properties":{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 22 at 3:24PM MDT until August 22 at 6:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorth Central Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 630 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 324 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area.\nBetween 1 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nIndian Creek, Willow Creek, Garber Creek, South Platte River,\nMiddle Garber Creek, Rainbow Creek, Pine Creek, West Bear Creek,\nDeer Creek, Plum Creek, Big Dry Creek, Bear Creek and North\nGarber Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHighlands Ranch, Littleton, Roxborough Park, Louviers, Chatfield\nReservoir, Sprucewood, Kassler and Columbine.","ends":"2026-08-22T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.79babdd62d6ef165ae91cdad79407999210da5fc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.79babdd62d6ef165ae91cdad79407999210da5fc.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-107.56,38.15],[-107.57,38.14],[-107.56,38.13],[-107.56,38.1],[-107.55,38.08],[-107.56,38.06],[-107.59,38.06],[-107.62,38.04],[-107.68,38.03],[-107.72,38.1],[-107.71,38.11],[-107.72,38.15],[-107.65,38.18],[-107.65,38.2],[-107.58,38.21],[-107.57,38.19],[-107.56,38.16],[-107.56,38.15]]]},"properties":{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 22 at 2:49PM MDT until August 22 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Gold Mountain burn scar in...\nNorthwestern Hinsdale County in southwestern Colorado...\nEast Central Ouray County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthwestern Gunnison County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 545 PM MDT.\n\n* At 249 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Gold Mountain Burn Scar. Between 0.2 and 0.5\ninches of rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 3\ninches in 1 hour. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.2 to 0.5 inches\nare possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly. Excessive rainfall over the burn scar\nwill result in debris flow moving through the Cutler Creek, Dexter\nCreek, and Cow Creek. The debris flow can consist of rock, mud,\nvegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Gold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nGold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPortland, Ouray, and the Highway 550 corridor.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; Ouray, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7a16d4759a53e25fd337f647dfb1304677b1572c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7a16d4759a53e25fd337f647dfb1304677b1572c.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-104.81,39.36],[-104.84,39.32],[-104.82,39.3],[-104.73,39.3],[-104.69,39.34],[-104.71,39.38],[-104.76,39.38],[-104.79,39.37],[-104.81,39.36]]]},"properties":{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 22 at 2:13PM MDT until August 22 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"FFWBOU\n\nThe National Weather Service in Denver has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 500 PM MDT.\n\n* At 213 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between\n1 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts\nup to 0.5 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, gulches,\nroads, and poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nCastlewood Canyon.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nCherry Creek, Willow Creek, East Plum Creek and Lake Gulch.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.caa774c820a22455f92d2ad6d63655b8379725e7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.caa774c820a22455f92d2ad6d63655b8379725e7.001.1"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-105.048599,38.198711],[-105.0439,38.198711],[-105.040695,38.196011],[-104.973595,38.150913],[-104.956093,38.133511],[-104.9459,38.11161],[-104.944496,38.107311],[-104.9459,38.095612],[-104.954697,38.085411],[-104.961899,38.081112],[-104.967796,38.069412],[-104.9692,38.054913],[-104.966293,38.043312],[-104.961899,38.030212],[-104.944496,38.012711],[-104.937195,38.004013],[-104.9226,37.996712],[-104.918297,37.98941],[-104.905197,37.976311],[-104.905197,37.958912],[-104.881897,37.948711],[-104.881897,37.935612],[-104.905197,37.909412],[-104.902596,37.887413],[-104.901199,37.873413],[-104.901894,37.869114],[-104.899399,37.858311],[-104.899895,37.847412],[-104.911293,37.837013],[-104.911797,37.821812],[-104.916199,37.812912],[-104.924599,37.798111],[-104.928497,37.786713],[-104.939301,37.777714],[-104